From: Luisyr <106528106+luisyr1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:05:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/11] arm64: dts: komodo: describe the MAX77779 fuel gauge
 (read-only)

The stock komodo DTBO (board_id 0x60806, rev 0x10000) has max77779fg@36
on hsi2c_6 (i2c@108d0000), status okay. Bind it to the in-tree read-only
max77779_battery driver (CONFIG_BATTERY_MAX77779=m), which never writes
the gauge and refuses it if FSTAT says the model is not ready. No
interrupt (the stock one goes through the MAX77779 PMIC's interrupt
controller, which has no driver here); the driver polls.

Tested on komodo.
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts    | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
index 539419c20..2855d8d0c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-komodo.dts
@@ -382,6 +382,22 @@ connector {
 			try-power-role = "sink";
 		};
 	};
+
+	/*
+	 * The MAX77779 fuel gauge (stock DTBO entry board_id 0x60806:
+	 * max77779fg@36 on hsi2c_6, "maxim,max77779fg-i2c"). Read-only:
+	 * max77779_battery writes no register and refuses a gauge whose
+	 * firmware model is not ready. The 2 mOhm shunt is the MAX77779
+	 * reference value used on the Pixel 9a (tegu); check it against
+	 * charge_full_design (stock google,chg-battery-capacity = 4942 mAh).
+	 * No power-supplies link yet: the charger node does not exist, and
+	 * a link to a missing supply defers the probe forever.
+	 */
+	fuel-gauge@36 {
+		compatible = "maxim,max77779-fg";
+		reg = <0x36>;
+		shunt-resistor-micro-ohms = <2000>;
+	};
 };
 
 &usi2_hsi0 {
